From 548fdf30da15b236f8ddc1553f4692eb9f5cb5c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venkit Kasiviswanathan <venkit@nexthop.ai>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 20:25:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bgpd, zebra: compute BGP PIC backup paths for fast failover

Backport of FRRouting/frr PR #21814 ("bgpd: compute BGP backup paths
for fast failover") onto frr-10.7.1.

Add support for computing one or more backup paths in BGP based on a
per AFI/SAFI configuration, and publish them to zebra as a route-level
backup pool that is engaged only when all primary nexthops are down
(BGP PIC-Local).

bgpd:

* When BGP_CONFIG_BACKUP_PATH is set, after best-path selection BGP
  picks the next-best path that is not in the multipath set as the
  backup. With BGP_CONFIG_BACKUP_PATH_ECMP, equal-cost candidates
  beyond the first backup are also marked, bounded by maximum-paths.
  Selected paths carry BGP_PATH_BACKUP; BGP_PATH_BACKUP_CHG drives a
  re-announce to zebra so the RIB stays in sync without bestpath churn.
* CLI: "install backup-path" and "install backup-path ecmp" under the
  ipv4/ipv6 unicast address-family, plus their "no" forms, which
  schedule a backup-path flush so stale BGP_PATH_BACKUP flags are
  cleared.
* show bgp: backup paths are flagged with the new "B" status code and
  "backup": true in JSON. route_vty_out / route_vty_out_tag /
  route_vty_out_tmp gain an afi argument so the indicator renders
  correctly across unicast, EVPN and VPN call sites.
* bgp_zebra_announce_parse_nexthop() encodes the backup paths into
  api->backup_nexthops[] (zapi_nexthop_init() on every slot) and sets
  ZAPI_MESSAGE_BACKUP_NEXTHOPS plus ZAPI_MESSAGE_BACKUP_ALL_PRIMARIES_DOWN.
  Primary nexthops carry no HAS_BACKUP / backup_idx[] in this mode.

ZAPI (lib/zclient.h):

* New message bit ZAPI_MESSAGE_BACKUP_ALL_PRIMARIES_DOWN. When set
  together with ZAPI_MESSAGE_BACKUP_NEXTHOPS, backup_nexthops[] is a
  route-scope pool engaged only when every primary is down. This is
  orthogonal to the existing per-NH protection (TI-LFA / IP-FRR) that
  uses HAS_BACKUP + backup_idx[].

zebra:

* New NHE flag NEXTHOP_GROUP_BACKUP_ALL_PRIMARIES_DOWN, set by
  zread_route_add() from the ZAPI bit, propagated by zebra_nhe_copy()
  and included in zebra_nhg_hash_key()/zebra_nhg_hash_equal() so
  route-level pools never alias per-NH backup groups.
* The recursive resolver does not merge per-NH backups into a resolved
  NHE flagged route-level.
* dplane: new dplane_ctx_get_backup_all_primaries_down() accessor so
  dplane providers can tell the two semantics apart.
* show ip route: renders the route-level backup pool after the
  primaries and adds "backupAllPrimariesDown": true to JSON.

Topotests:

* bgp_backup: single backup path selection, re-selection on interface
  state change, BGP and zebra text/JSON rendering.
* bgp_backup_ecmp: ECMP backup paths, the no-ecmp transition and
  disablement via "no install backup-path".
* bgp_backup_recursive: backup nexthop that requires recursive
  resolution through an underlay route.
* all_protocol_startup: show_bgp_*.ref legends updated for the new
  "B Backup" status code.

Signed-off-by: Venkit Kasiviswanathan <venkit@nexthop.ai>
